    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0373" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg297"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20/735: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-18T13:00:00-05:00">March 18, 1935—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Press dispatches earlier in day give account of Simon’s speech in Commons
                    about note<anchor n="38" xml:id="d231-f1"/> to Germany. Very important that we
                    should know nature of it as we are without any background or other official
                    information from London for our guidance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d231-f1" n="38" xml:id="d231-f1-content">
                <p>British Cmd. 4848, Germany No. 1 (1935): <hi rendition="#italic">Note Delivered
                        by His Majesty’s, Ambassador in Berlin to the German Government on Maxell
                        18, 1935</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
